---
import UxCard from "../UxCard.astro";
---

<UxCard
  id="A-14"
  domain="Accessibility"
  domainClass="a-a"
  title=`Icon Buttons Need<br/>Accessible Names`
  rule=`<strong>The accessible name is what screen readers announce.</strong> For icon-only buttons the visual label is the icon: which is meaningless to AT. Pick the strategy that fits: <code>aria-label</code> for standalone icons, visually-hidden text when you need translatable strings, <code>aria-labelledby</code> when a visible label exists nearby.`
>
<div class="fc-5 a14-visual">
<div class="vis-box-neutral">
<div class="mono-section-head" style="margin-bottom:4px;">Three ways to name an icon button</div>
<div class="fc-3">
<div class="vis-label-dark">aria-label="Search"</div>
<div class="vis-label-dark">aria-labelledby="visible-text-id"</div>
<div class="vis-label-dark">&lt;span class="sr-only"&gt;Search&lt;/span&gt;</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="vis-label-bad-cap">title="" alone doesn't count: it's not announced reliably</div>
</div>
</UxCard>